<title>UK: INTERVIEW-Redland French aggregates for sale.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW-Redland French aggregates for sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Building materials group Redland Plc said on Thursday it had put its French aggregates business up for sale and that it was currently in talks with several interested parties.</p>
<p>Robert Napier, chief executive, told Reuters in an interview &quot;Our aggregates business is for sale. We are in active discussions with a number of interested parties.&quot; The business called Granulats has a book value of 310 million stg and employs 2,500 people.</p>
</text>
